            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was so simple and delicious! I used light cream cheese, half garlic powder, half minced garlic and fresh chives instead of dried. This was great spread over fresh bagels and as a dip for carrot and celery sticks - a definite keeper."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Linda Farrell"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used 1 individual package of WW (weight watchers) cream cheese spread, 1/8 tsp garlic powder and 1/8 tsp dried chives. Used instead of mayo on my turkey sandwich for lunch. Would be great melted over pasta, on garlic bread and even over fish. The possibilities are endless!",
            "datePublished": "2011-03-12T11:18:24.680Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Trish"
            },
            "reviewBody": "How easy does it get? I only made half the recipe as a trial. We love garlic so I used the garlic powder along with finely minced fresh garlic. It is good and will be enjoyed on bagels for the most part. I will make this again, in full next time.",
            "datePublished": "2021-03-03T23:23:04.843Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made a half recipe of this, using reduced fat cream cheese. After tasting it, I added in more chives and garlic powder. It just needed more. We ate this for lunch spread on whole wheat bread and made into a tomato and lettuce sandwich. I love the idea. Next time, I'll add onion powder, too, I think.",
            "datePublished": "2011-10-01T11:41:54.260Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MrsPolk"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used some fresh green onion from the garden as well as some fresh garlic in addition to garlic salt (didn't have any garlic powder). Very tasty! Spread it on some butter crackers and top with a slice or two of cucumber and some dried dill - so delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2017-07-20T17:23:45.227Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Chey1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've been making this for a while and am finally reviewing it as I was searching for another of my favorite recipes. This is absolutely the best basic easy versatile cream cheese spread ever! It's delicious as is - I sometimes add chopped cooked bacon. I seriously cannot understand buying cream cheese spread when easy yummy recipes exist that will always taste better than store bought. ..... just sayin'..... : )",
            "datePublished": "2016-06-28T01:57:44.980Z"
          },
          {
